sam: Quick triage: PR touching SDK examples for streaming + pagination. Found two things in the rendered docs: the Python example resumes incorrectly when a transient error triggers a retry, and the TS/Go snippets don't show closing the stream. Can we align examples and add a note about resume tokens being idempotent?

lina: Can you drop the minimal failing snippet?

sam: Python repro (simplified):
```python
# if retry restarts the async iterator, progress can be lost
async def get_all(client):
    cursor = None
    while True:
        try:
            async for p in client.stream_pages(cursor=cursor):
                handle(p.items)
                cursor = p.next_cursor
            break
        except TransientError:
            await asyncio.sleep(0.2)
            # without persisting cursor outside, we may restart from older state
            continue
```

devnull-bot: :link: Link-checker: detected old path /docs/streaming/guide -> 404; recommend /docs/streaming/v2.

owen: Suggested Python guidance: always persist the resume cursor outside the generator and pass it into the request on retry. Also show a tiny stateful loop example and a note about idempotent resume tokens.

owen: Proposed TS pattern (adds explicit close):
```ts
const s = client.streamPages({ cursor });
try {
  for await (const page of s) {
    handle(page.items);
    cursor = page.next_cursor;
  }
} finally {
  await s.close();
}
```

mira: For Go, we should demonstrate a small retry wrapper that leaves the cursor string in the outer scope and uses it to resume. Also mention to prefer server-side resume tokens over client-side offsets.

lina: I'll update the PR: add the Python note + TS try/finally + Go resume example + swap out the broken link. Can @owen and @mira review quickly?

owen: Will review in 30m, will also add a small markdown test asserting the sample contains "stream.close" and "resume token" text.

sam: Thanks — if reviewers sign off, aim to merge before tomorrow AM. Small doc-only changes. :shipit:
